00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:17.160
The method suits capital goods companies that show steady earnings visibility and keep payout ratios under 60 percent.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:30.060
Pressure can build if dividend growth slows or if capital rotates toward faster growing areas instead. The screen should only trigger when trading volume clears the 20-day average to reduce the chance of false signals.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:36.720
The 33 percent gap originates from an automated model refreshed after every dividend announcement.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:45.220
Cross checking the implied value difference against the latest quarterly free cash flow report helps size any potential exposure properly.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:53.960
This approach skips momentum-driven names and focuses instead on cases where the dividend lift itself improves the intrinsic value math.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:03:01.160
Picture adding a 3 percent Bitcoin slice to a TFSA during a stretch when ETF inflows looked favorable.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:10.900
The fill occurs at spot but the real cost includes any premium or discount to net asset value plus the management expense ratio that covers custody.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:20.900
Vehicles such as BTCX and ETHX allow the exposure inside a TFSA without extra foreign exchange steps or personal key management.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:32.600
Portfolio math indicates that a 1-5 percent satellite position can lift the overall sharp ratio because Bitcoin tends to show 0.2-0.3 correlation with equities.

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:40.640
The correlation tends to rise mainly during liquidity events so professionals review the 30-day rolling figure before increasing size.

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:45.680
Many retail accounts skip that check and treat the sleeve as a permanent diversifier.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:52.600
The usual error is to label any allocation above 0 as either too dangerous or the inevitable future.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:59.540
Treating crypto as a satellite holding that gets reviewed once a year against the rest of the portfolio keeps the size in check.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:08.140
When the 30-day correlation moves above 0.6 the diversification effect weakens and the sleeve should be scaled back to target.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:16.740
Using the TFSA wrapper adds an advantage because gains inside the account avoid capital gains inclusion and superficial loss tracking.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:27.380
Keeping the range at 1-5 percent means a 50 percent drawdown in the crypto portion still leaves total portfolio volatility inside most stated risk limits.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:34.000
Annual rebalancing forces a deliberate reset rather than letting price moves shift the weight over time.

